{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","externalID":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift#L91","fileName":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift"}},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of the Segment spec’s batch call, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to Segment, RudderStack, Customer.io Data Pipelines, or another endpoint that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes Segment’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v1\/batch"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"]]},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with one of the factories, which fill in the endpoint, the credentials’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header field, this encoder and its limits:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one member, ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an array","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of track calls, one per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The standard context, in the spec’s field names (below), and "},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"text":", in RudderStack’s calls alone","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, in UTC","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"\"track\"","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call, no traits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no "},{"code":"context.device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An endpoint counts a user per "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its anonymous users are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own anonymous user, linked to nothing: the spec rejects a call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with neither a "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" nor an "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its session, so it goes out with the "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicates calls by "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over about the last 24 hours, and drops most duplicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than all, so a recovered record Segment had already stored before the app ended is most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s references don’t say whether they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicate. The record’s vendor identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in every call, which the spec reads as the user’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Segment records no address from the request. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" member from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the request unless the call has one, even when ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is set, and passes it on to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Customer.io’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes the place of the address it reads from an HTTP","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. No call to Segment or Customer.io carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which their specs don’t have.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"originalTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"channel"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent. Without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":" the endpoint takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, uncorrected for the device’s clock; it is left out on purpose, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried request sends the same body again, whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":" would be the first attempt’s."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"RudderStack, whose references list all three as required, fills them in from when it received"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", the bundle identifier, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"},{"type":"text","text":", each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"; no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"type":"text","text":" when all three are"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"model"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"text":", the platform as Segment’s Swift library names it: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ios"},{"text":" for a phone or pad, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"macos"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tvos"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"watchos"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visionos"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"cellular","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whether the connection is each"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name is one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices, one whose event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one too large for a call (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" returns them as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UTF-8 bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://SegmentSpecEncoding/documentation/SegmentSpecEncoding/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder/Failure":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/segmentspecencoding\/segmentspecbatchencoder\/failure","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Failure"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Failure"}],"title":"